":"Root cause evidence, read from the Windows sweep job logs of runs 43820680079, 43871224211 and the b4e0d01b649 scheduled run (2026-11-15/16). Every failure uses a POSIX-only API on Windows with no Windows path:\n\n1. Product, gate admission: `src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py:25-28` imports `fcntl` directly (flock at :244, :270) and disarms the concurrency cap when it is absent (:333-336, reason \"advisory locking (fcntl) unavailable\"). Both `test_gate_admission_09da.py` failures assert on that marker. The store already has a portable leg with a Windows `msvcrt.locking` branch, `rebar._store.lock_kernel` (`take_exclusive`/`release_exclusive`/`leg_name`, `src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py:111-156`).\n2. Product, grounding harness: `run_in_worker` maps a crash to `parse_error` only for a negative exit code (`src/rebar/grounding/harness.py:385-395`). A native crash on Windows exits with a positive NTSTATUS code (e.g. 0xC0000005), so it would land in `other`. The payload `tests/unit/grounding/_worker_payloads.py:52-65` sends itself `signal.SIGKILL`, absent on Windows (worker \"raised: AttributeError\").\n3. Collection: `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py:201` uses `-signal.SIGKILL` in a module-level parametrize; the collection error (`ERROR tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py - AttributeError: module 'signal' has no attribute 'SIGKILL'`) is the only error in the logs of `test_ci_workflow_parity.py::test_make_test_never_selects_a_live_test_even_with_jira_credentials_set` and `test_collection_isolation_guard.py::test_the_live_unit_tier_collects_clean`.\n4. Test stub: `tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py:83-87` swaps `_proc.subprocess` for a SimpleNamespace with only `Popen`/`DEVNULL`; on Windows `_proc._detach_kwargs` (`src/rebar/_proc.py:112-121`) reads `DETACHED_PROCESS` from it (4 tests); `:123-124` assert POSIX kwargs unconditionally.\n5. POSIX-only legs exercised without a capability guard: fcntl-leg tests patching `_kernel.fcntl.flock` while it is None (`test_lock_stale_reclaim.py` 6, `test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py` 2); the fcntl control (`test_fcntl_import_guard.py`); `resource` reads (`test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py` 2; product already returns None without `resource`, `src/rebar/llm/peak_rss.py:40-48`); signal-killed children (`test_live_dc_pass_health.py` 2, `test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py` 1); in-process SIGTERM handler grace (`test_mcp_http_transport.py`, `assert 15 == 0`: on Windows `os.kill(pid, SIGTERM)` is TerminateProcess with exit 15, no handler runs); `os.getuid` (`tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py:72,92`, which runs the Linux host script `infra/scripts/materialize-gerrit-jgit-config.sh` that chowns to uid:gid) and `os.geteuid` (`tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py:517`).","timestamp":1795039171332145673},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit 3436 (3ff84ebc693). make verify: 21,404 passed, 1 failed (test_model_classes.py::test_a_finished_gate_drive_releases_its_event_loop[raised], the known host-load flake tracked by unselfish-finnicky-whooper, unrelated); the integration tier, which that failure stopped make from reaching, was run separately: 226 passed, 2 skipped. Portability: new paths use msvcrt via lock_kernel and os._exit, both present on Windows; no new POSIX-only API.","timestamp":1795049200354576155},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged as 4aeb9c0fe23 (Gerrit 3436). First Windows sweep with it, run 44456347985 (job 135332660982, main at ab323f7df0c): every removed posix-api line passed or skipped except 3. (1, 2) The 2 new `test_a_crash_exit_is_described_on_both_platforms[-9-*]` cases expected \"SIGKILL\", but `signal.Signals` has no SIGKILL member on Windows, so the name is \"signal 9\"; test expectation fixed. (3) `test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py::test_orchestrator_degrade_key_unregenerable_records_unsigned` no longer fails on `os.geteuid`; it now reaches a gate-snapshot path longer than MAX_PATH (\"Filename too long\"), so its line moves to `max-path.args` (halfcrazed-rubbly-whimbrel's class). Follow-up Gerrit 3443 (c3f9c1d1621); make verify passed in full, integration tier 226 passed.","timestamp":1795072409090761997}],"created_at":1794857643240118451,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d828e701-850a-40f2-a8ba-73c1143ff56a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"56607a75-2fb2-445f-b9f5-1169d92ec142","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c7f7-f539-6de8-4afd"},{"link_uuid":"c085b662-19b1-4852-bcb6-65eb02b57c06","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"41d3-2eb9-71d3-4ca6"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects tests known to fail on Windows through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args`. This bug owns that file: 27 `--deselect` lines plus `--ignore=tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py`. Each failure uses a POSIX-only API on Windows with no Windows path. The per-test evidence (job logs of runs 43820680079, 43871224211 and the `b4e0d01b649` run) is in the ticket comment \"Root cause evidence\"; in short:\n\n- Product: `src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py:25-28` imports `fcntl` and disarms the gate cap on Windows (`:333-336`), although `rebar._store.lock_kernel` (`take_exclusive`/`release_exclusive`/`leg_name`, `src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py:111-156`) already has a Windows `msvcrt` leg.\n- Product: `src/rebar/grounding/harness.py:385-395` treats only a negative exit code as a crash; a Windows native crash exits with a positive NTSTATUS code (e.g. `0xC0000005`). The payload `tests/unit/grounding/_worker_payloads.py:52-65` uses `signal.SIGKILL`.\n- `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py:201` uses `-signal.SIGKILL` at collection time; that collection error is the sole cause of the `test_ci_workflow_parity.py` and `test_collection_isolation_guard.py` failures.\n- `tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py:83-87` stubs `subprocess` without the Windows constants `src/rebar/_proc.py:112-121` reads.\n- The other tests exercise POSIX-only legs (fcntl, `resource`, signal death, SIGTERM handlers, `os.getuid`/`os.geteuid`) with no capability guard.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the product where Windows has a real equivalent; guard tests on the missing capability where the behaviour is POSIX-only by design. This keeps every product guarantee and follows the precedent of `lock_kernel` for the store lock.\n\n- `gate_admission`: drop the `fcntl` import; take and drop slots with `lock_kernel.take_exclusive` (non-blocking on both legs) and `release_exclusive`. Disarm only when `lock_kernel.leg_name() == \"none\"`, reason \"no exclusive file-lock primitive (fcntl or msvcrt) available\". On Windows the cap is then enforced.\n- `grounding.harness`: move exit-status classification into a small pure function that also treats a Windows exit code with NTSTATUS error severity (`>= 0xC0000000`) as a crash (`parse_error`, hex code in `detail`). `hard_crash` keeps SIGKILL on POSIX; on Windows it exits with the access-violation status (`os._exit(-1073741819)`, seen by the parent as `0xC0000005`), the status the harness observes for a real native crash.\n- `test_bridge_runner_spawn.py:201`: literal returncode `-9`.\n- `test_spawn_detached.py`: stub built from `vars(subprocess)` with `Popen` overridden; assert the platform's own detach kwargs.\n- Guards: `skipif(_kernel.fcntl is None)` (fcntl-leg tests); `pytest.importorskip(\"fcntl\")` / `(\"resource\")`; `skipif(not hasattr(signal, \"SIGKILL\"))`; `skipif(os.name == \"nt\")` on the SIGTERM-grace test (Windows `os.kill` is TerminateProcess); `skipif(not hasattr(os, \"getuid\"))` on the Linux host-script test; `not hasattr(os, \"geteuid\") or os.geteuid() == 0` selects the existing simulated branch in `test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py`.\n- Delete `posix-api.args` and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` (`tests/unit/test_windows_sweep_deselect.py` keeps them in step).\n\nPortability: no new POSIX-only API. New paths use `msvcrt` via `lock_kernel` and `os._exit`, both present on Windows. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py`, `src/rebar/grounding/harness.py`\n- `tests/unit/grounding/_worker_payloads.py`, `tests/unit/grounding/test_harness.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py` (no-leg disarm test patches `lock_kernel.fcntl`/`msvcrt` to `None`; the non-blocking spy test spies `lock_kernel.take_exclusive`)\n- `tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py`, `tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py`, `tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py`, `tests/unit/test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py`, `tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py`, `tests/unit/test_live_dc_pass_health.py`, `tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py`, `tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py`, `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py`, `tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args` (deleted), `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\n- New harness classifier tests, run on every platform: a negative exit maps to `parse_error` naming the signal; `0xC0000005` on Windows maps to `parse_error` naming the hex status; exit `3` stays `other`.\n- Gate admission on POSIX: existing congestion and release tests pass through `lock_kernel`; failure path: with both legs patched to `None` admission disarms with the new reason.\n- After merge, a dispatched `sweep (windows)` run on main.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change, including the new harness classifier tests.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-api.args` names a test that passed (or skipped with a capability reason) in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run, with `posix-api.args` and its `@` reference removed.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py","reason":"take slots through the portable lock_kernel leg"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/harness.py","reason":"classify Windows NTSTATUS crash exits as parse_error"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/_worker_payloads.py","reason":"Windows crash payload"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_harness.py","reason":"classifier unit tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py","reason":"adapt disarm and spy tests to lock_kernel"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_bridge_runner_spawn.py","reason":"collectable on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py","reason":"stub carries platform constants"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_lock_stale_reclaim.py","reason":"fcntl capability guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084.py","reason":"fcntl capability guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fcntl_import_guard.py","reason":"fcntl capability guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_peak_rss_9ea3.py","reason":"resource capability guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_live_dc_pass_health.py","reason":"SIGKILL capability guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_external_mutation_diagnostics.py","reason":"SIGKILL capability guard"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py","reason":"geteuid capability guard"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py","reason":"SIGTERM handler grace is POSIX-only"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_gerrit_object_store_repair.py","reason":"Linux host script needs uid:gid"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-api.args","reason":"deleted once empty"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"drop the posix-api argfile reference"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","41d3-2eb9-71d3-4ca6"],["relates_to","c7f7-f539-6de8-4afd"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"97f7c5df-c9a1-4132-9801-f44a6236d9cd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"4357-c54c-71b0-4bb4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: POSIX-only APIs used without a Windows path (28 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e88b0a07-750d-4e73-81b4-57a2dfc6ae21","c6036554-821f-48d8-8d32-1147f3b281ea","d2cc6553-19aa-44d1-a673-5c862be3f332","68522793-4aff-4ac9-bd79-565c1c57fcc7","034ec0b4-88ca-4766-b37b-0122787ebc89","97f7c5df-c9a1-4132-9801-f44a6236d9cd","901372fd-2ed4-4ebf-90be-57675a1ab5c3","8fcea562-40a1-4b3a-b9e3-7440a9117cd8","56607a75-2fb2-445f-b9f5-1169d92ec142","013cd5e1-19b1-48c5-95a1-b7e6bf94301e","c085b662-19b1-4852-bcb6-65eb02b57c06"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795072970492829273,"uuid":"355e3ff2-fecb-4031-8a6d-c92e3a054cdb"}
